# [10.5.7]('') Publishing websites

R Markdown websites are static HTML sites that can be deployed to any standard web server. 
All site content (generated documents and supporting files) are copied into the _site directory, so deployment is simply a matter of moving that directory to the appropriate directory of a web server. [cite paper online]

## Site generator

Building static websites requires a "site generator" to configure the site files and assoicated information in a manner that can be used to search and present the data and resources that have been curated.

